# @kintsugi/fracture/bilateral_arm_redundant — the OPERATIONAL fracture
# species that names the pattern "a `bilateral` block was declared in
# a shard AND the reflective evaluator would handle its dispatch, but
# a hand-typed arm at `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs` still discharges the
# same action ref by direct `if action == "@X/Y.name" { ... contains(
# "<sentinel>") ... }` string-check." The arm's continued existence
# IS the fracture; its byte-range deletion IS the resolution; the
# roomba composition dispatches the resolution as one turn in the
# @roomba × @kintsugi @metalogue at @algebra/metalogue altitude.
#
# Species under @kintsugi/fracture at reflective-corpus altitude.
# Fifteenth landed sibling to the fourteen existing fracture bodies
# (angle_to_paren, cold_compile_within_tolerance, dark_count_monotone,
# docblock_extractive, docblock_incoherent, docblock_ungrounded, gate,
# keyword, operator_match, parent_cycle, partials_align, relocate,
# restart_storm, symbol_lift). Same shape: typed carrier + detect
# action + resolution action + composed bilateral discipline.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Alex 2026-07-16 /loop directive verbatim (session-crystallizing):
#     "collapse the Rust surface using mirror's roomba. Minimal
#      surface in rust/. Then the roomba starts to eat the bootstrap
#      for breakfast and grows the substrate. That's the roomba
#      commit diffs I wanna see. Deleted Rust. Added mirror."
#
#   The compiler authors the deletion commit itself. `mirror`
#   <mirror@spectral.engineer>, not Reed. This species is the
#   fracture-body substrate the roomba walks into and mends.
#
# - Canonical spec: `docs/specs/kintsugi-fracture-bilateral-arm-
#   redundant.md` (Mara THIS-tick; the detection algorithm +
#   resolution algorithm + composition graph + landing plan for
#   Reed's follow-up).
#
# - Math foundation: `docs/math/kintsugi/fracture/bilateral-arm-
#   redundant.md` (Mara THIS-tick; the formal redundancy predicate +
#   retirement invariants + termination proof + Connes-triple angle).
#
# === Audit chain ===
#
# The bilateral-arm retirement arc has landed six ticks ahead of this
# species; this species names the fracture whose per-arm resolution
# closes the arc:
#
#   1. `a0f4d3f/9a77361/701828a` (Mara) — the
#      `@epistemologic/pact/bilateral` shape: bilateral typed carrier +
#      canonical spec + math foundation naming the reflective corpus
#      shape the ~30 hand-typed apply_h::act arms shadow.
#
#   2. `61c9051/21fc211` (Reed via subagent) — the reflective
#      evaluator + corpus loader in `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs`. The
#      bilateral corpus is checked FIRST; the resolver falls through
#      to the legacy hand-typed arms only when the corpus misses.
#      This is the substrate-honest half of the retirement: the
#      floor now dispatches reflectively.
#
#   3. `71bb9b2` (Mara) — Landing 1 bite 1: four `bilateral` blocks
#      added to `shards/spectral/signature.mirror` naming the four
#      predicates' sentinels + arities in shard-decl form.
#
#   4. `06f14f5` (Reed via subagent) — Landing 5 bite 1: retired the
#      four `@spectral/signature` hand-typed arms from
#      `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs`. Reflective dispatch handled them;
#      6/6 tests passed; net -32 LOC. First empirical witness that
#      the retirement discipline works.
#
# THIS TICK closes the substrate-honest loop: the six preceding ticks
# established that Reed can retire arms manually with subagent help;
# this species mints the fracture body the roomba detects + resolves
# autonomously. Reed-authored retirement was Alex-authoring by proxy.
# `mirror <mirror@spectral.engineer>` authoring — the compiler-as-
# author — is the terminal shape. This species is the substrate the
# terminal shape composes over.
#
# === The load-bearing claim ===
#
# For every entry `(action_ref, sentinel)` in the bilateral corpus
# `load_bilateral_corpus(ctx)` returns:
#
#   IF there exists a hand-typed arm in `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs`
#   matching `if action == "<action_ref>" { ... .contains("<sentinel>") ... }`
#
#   THEN that arm IS a `bilateral_arm_redundant` fracture:
#     - its work is done by the reflective corpus (61c9051/21fc211)
#     - its continued existence is duplication of the shard-decl
#     - its discharge (Pass|Fail on the same argument list) is
#       byte-equal to the reflective evaluator's discharge
#     - its byte-range deletion strictly decreases `rust_loc(after)`
#       while preserving `sbec(after) = sbec(before)` and
#       `test_pass_rate(after) = test_pass_rate(before) = 100%`
#
# The species names this fracture pattern at reflective-corpus
# altitude. The detect action reads the bilateral corpus + `apply_h.rs`
# bytes and emits a `[redundant_arm_record]` naming every arm the
# resolver can safely delete. The collapse action reads one record,
# byte-deletes the arm's line range via `@io/fs.mutate_at` (with
# empty replacement), commits via `@io/git.commit` as `mirror
# <mirror@spectral.engineer>`.
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word discovery ===
#
# The `@io/fs.mutate_at(p: path, pos: source_position, replacement:
# bytes) -> imperfect` action landed 2026-07-15 at Mara Landing 7 IS
# already the byte-boundary-precision splice primitive this species
# needs. Line-range deletion IS `mutate_at` with:
#
#   pos.byte_offset  = start of the arm's `if action == ...` line
#   pos.byte_length  = end of the closing `}` — start
#   replacement      = "" (empty bytes)
#
# The word was there. No `@nl.line_range_delete` mint is needed;
# @io/fs.mutate_at at empty-replacement altitude IS line-range
# deletion. Substrate-honest per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-
# the-word]] (~73rd landed instance).
#
# === The detection surface ===
#
# The `detect` action reads the corpus + `apply_h.rs` bytes; for each
# `(action_ref, sentinel)` in the corpus, greps for the arm pattern.
# When found, emits a `redundant_arm_record` naming:
#
#   action_ref       — the shard-decl'd action string (e.g.,
#                       "@spectral/signature.signature_integrity")
#   apply_h_path     — the file the arm lives in
#                       ("bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs")
#   arm_line_start   — the first line of the arm's if-block
#   arm_line_end     — the last line of the arm's closing `}`
#   sentinel         — the shard-decl'd sentinel byte-string; MUST
#                       equal the `.contains(...)` argument on the
#                       arm's guard line (bilateral discipline)
#   arm_bytes        — the arm's byte-range content (audit trail;
#                       what the resolver deletes)
#
# The detect action's return is a `[redundant_arm_record]` — one
# record per redundant arm; empty list when the fixed-point holds
# (no arm shadows any bilateral in the corpus).
#
# === The resolution surface ===
#
# The `collapse` action reads one `redundant_arm_record`; discharges:
#
#   1. Read `apply_h.rs` bytes via `@io/fs.read(record.apply_h_path)`.
#   2. Compute `source_position` from arm_line_start/arm_line_end
#      byte offsets (line-to-byte via the byte-visible line table).
#   3. Call `@io/fs.mutate_at(apply_h_path, source_position, empty_bytes)`
#      to byte-delete the arm; POSIX-atomic write-to-temp + rename
#      preserves the file's other bytes.
#   4. Call `@io/git.commit(message, "mirror <mirror@spectral.engineer>",
#      allow_empty=false)` with a commit message naming the retired
#      arm + the shard-decl'd bilateral it shadows + the byte-count
#      delta.
#
# The verdict returned is `@glass.verdict`:
#   pass                 — arm deleted; file rewritten byte-atomically;
#                           commit landed under mirror-authorship.
#   partial(confidence)  — arm deleted but with residual (e.g.,
#                           surrounding whitespace drift; needs cargo
#                           fmt in follow-up tick; commit landed).
#   failure(reason)      — deletion NOT applied; file preserved
#                           byte-identically (path missing; position
#                           out of range; git commit refused). No
#                           substrate mutation.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl):
#   @kintsugi/fracture          — family-root; fifteenth sibling
#                                   species under the fracture pattern
#   @kintsugi/consent           — verdict authority per
#                                   `[[feedback-morphism-carrier-per-
#                                   feedback]]`; collapse emits verdict
#                                   the outer kintsugi loop reads
#   @kintsugi/morphism          — the morphism carrier the fracture
#                                   emits (deletion morphism at byte
#                                   altitude)
#   @epistemologic/pact/bilateral — the corpus this species reads;
#                                   the sentinel-per-arm-verification
#                                   discipline
#   @kintsugi/roomba            — the walker that dispatches this
#                                   species' detect action per pulse;
#                                   composition edge lands in Reed
#                                   follow-up tick A
#   @io/fs                       — mutate_at at empty-replacement =
#                                   line-range deletion; the byte-
#                                   boundary substrate
#   @io/git                      — commit under mirror-authorship;
#                                   the deletion is authored by the
#                                   compiler, not by Reed
#   @apply_h                     — the resolver whose hand-typed arms
#                                   are the fracture sites
#
# Consumers (compose over this species):
#   @kintsugi/roomba             — Reed tick A adds one composition
#                                    edge: on walk-step where a
#                                    `bilateral` block is encountered,
#                                    dispatch this species' detect
#                                    action
#   `mirror roomba --commit --collapse=bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs`
#                                — Reed tick C empirical run; the
#                                    compiler authors the deletion
#                                    commit itself
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain (this landing) ===
#
# 1. `@io/fs.mutate_at` (2026-07-15 Landing 7 by Mara) — the byte-
#    boundary splice primitive. Line-range deletion = empty
#    replacement; no `@nl.line_range_delete` mint needed.
#
# 2. `@io/git.commit(message, author, allow_empty)` (2026-06-24 by
#    Mara; @io/git species) — the commit surface. Authoring identity
#    is a first-class argument; `mirror <mirror@spectral.engineer>`
#    fits without new mechanism.
#
# 3. `@epistemologic/pact/bilateral.discharge(decl, args) -> verdict`
#    (a0f4d3f Mara this session) — the reflective evaluator surface.
#    The corpus lookup key IS the `action_ref` this species stores
#    in `redundant_arm_record`.
#
# 4. `@kintsugi/roomba.bump(position) -> kintsugi_dispatch`
#    (roomba.mirror additive cascade Alex 2026-07-16) — the walker's
#    fracture-emission trigger. This species is one target species
#    the bump dispatches to via `fracture_species` open enum.
#
# 5. `@glass.source_position` (2026-07-15 Landing per Mara ff8fbb1) —
#    the byte-precision splice-coordinate carrier the `collapse`
#    action passes to `mutate_at`.
#
# The word was there for every primitive this species composes over.
# ZERO new substrate machinery beyond the three artifacts
# (shard-decl + spec + math).
#
# === Bilateral discipline: this species dogfoods the shape it enforces ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-16 substrate-honest self-reference: the three
# bilateral predicates below use the `bilateral <name> { sentinel
# "..." arity 1 }` shape landed at `a0f4d3f`. This IS the mint
# consuming its own product — the species that resolves shadow arms
# declares its own predicates through the shape whose reflective
# dispatch REPLACES shadow arms. Substrate-honest self-reference at
# reflective-corpus altitude.
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] — this species IS a
#   shard-decl; the roomba composition edge reads the shard at parse
#   time via the reflective loader.
# [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]] — verdict is
#   `@glass.verdict`; source_position is `@glass.source_position`;
