prism @kintsugi/fracture/bilateral_arm_redundant {
  focus  redundant_arm
  project redundant_arm
  split  redundant_arm
  shift  redundant_arm
  settle redundant_arm
}

# === The redundant_arm_record carrier ===
#
# The typed record naming one hand-typed apply_h.rs arm shadowed by a
# bilateral corpus entry. Consumed by the `collapse` action; produced
# by the `detect` action. The unit-of-repair for the roomba's per-
# pulse fracture-emission at reflective-corpus altitude.
#
# Six fields (per the resolution surface's argument closure):
#
#   action_ref       — the shard-decl'd action string the arm and the
#                       corpus both dispatch on (e.g.,
#                       "@spectral/signature.signature_integrity").
#                       Content-addressed identity: two records with
#                       the same action_ref name the same fracture.
#
#   apply_h_path     — the file the arm lives in
#                       ("bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs" for the current
#                       arc; species accepts any future resolver
#                       file per composition).
#
#   arm_line_start   — the first line of the arm's `if action == ...`
#                       guard. Byte-visible from the source; the
#                       resolver reads via `@io/fs.read` at collapse
#                       time.
#
#   arm_line_end     — the last line of the arm's closing `}`. The
#                       inclusive end of the byte range to delete.
#
#   sentinel         — the shard-decl'd sentinel byte-string; MUST
#                       equal the `.contains(...)` argument on the
#                       arm's guard line. Bilateral discipline: the
#                       arm's runtime check IS the sentinel check;
#                       redundancy IS byte-equality between the
#                       arm's inline sentinel and the shard-decl'd
#                       sentinel.
#
#   arm_bytes        — the arm's byte-range content (audit trail;
#                       what the resolver deletes). Content-addressed
#                       for the roomba's kintsugi_dispatch record's
#                       morphism.content field.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (action_ref, apply_h_path,
# arm_line_start, arm_line_end, sentinel, arm_bytes). Two records
# name the same fracture iff all six fields byte-match.
type redundant_arm_record = {
  action_ref:      ref,
  apply_h_path:    ref,
  arm_line_start:  u32,
  arm_line_end:    u32,
  sentinel:        ref,
  arm_bytes:       ref,
}

# === arm_is_in_reflective_corpus — bilateral predicate (arity 1) ===
#
# Does the record's action_ref name a key in the bilateral corpus?
# The FIRST redundancy conjunct: if the reflective evaluator's corpus
# does NOT contain the arm's action ref, the arm is NOT redundant
# (its dispatch is uniquely served by the arm; deletion would break
# the resolver). The predicate discharges Pass iff the corpus lookup
# succeeds for the record's action_ref.
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: reads only byte-visible state
# (the corpus keyset via `load_bilateral_corpus(ctx)`; the record's
# action_ref field); no program semantics inspection.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `arm=in-reflective-corpus` — the byte-
# level substrate-decl'd marker. When the record's action_ref
# resolves to a bilateral declaration via the corpus loader, the
# realization layer stamps the sentinel; discharge is byte-equality
# on the ref.oid containment check per
# `@epistemologic/pact/bilateral.discharge`.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]];
# Reed follow-up tick B composes this via `apply_h::act` (the
# reflective evaluator handles this bilateral through its own corpus
# lookup by construction; the arm-is-in-corpus check IS a corpus
# `contains_key(action_ref)` operation lifted to bilateral altitude).
bilateral arm_is_in_reflective_corpus {
  sentinel "arm=in-reflective-corpus"
  arity    1
}
arm_is_in_reflective_corpus(record: redundant_arm_record) -> verdict { \ }

# === arm_matches_sentinel — bilateral predicate (arity 1) ===
#
# Does the record's `sentinel` field byte-equal the shard-decl'd
# sentinel the arm's `.contains(...)` line checks against? The SECOND
# redundancy conjunct: the reflective evaluator's discharge byte-
# equals the arm's discharge ONLY IF both check against the same
# sentinel. If the arm checks a DIFFERENT sentinel than the shard-
# decl declares, deletion would silently change the resolver's
# verdict on the same input — substrate-dishonest.
#
# The predicate discharges Pass iff:
#   corpus[record.action_ref].sentinel == record.sentinel   (byte-equality)
#
# The record's sentinel field IS the arm's inline `.contains(...)`
# argument extracted at detect time. Byte-equality between it and the
# corpus entry's sentinel is the guarantee that the arm's semantics
# IS the corpus entry's semantics.
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: reads only byte-visible state
# (two byte-strings compared for byte-equality); no program
# semantics.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `arm=matches-shard-sentinel` — the
# byte-level substrate-decl'd marker. When byte-equality holds, the
# realization layer stamps the sentinel; discharge is byte-equality.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked; realized by the reflective evaluator.
bilateral arm_matches_sentinel {
  sentinel "arm=matches-shard-sentinel"
  arity    1
}
arm_matches_sentinel(record: redundant_arm_record) -> verdict { \ }

# === arm_is_redundant_witnessing — composed bilateral (arity 1) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral. Passes iff BOTH sub-bilaterals
# discharge Pass on the same record:
#
#   arm_is_redundant_witnessing(record) :=
#     arm_is_in_reflective_corpus(record)
#     ∧ arm_matches_sentinel(record)
#
# Sibling to walk_witnessing at @kintsugi/roomba, home_witnessing at
# @peer/persistence, coherence_witnessing at @epistemologic/cybernetic/
# coherence — the composed-bilateral pattern at species-witnessing
# altitude. Two conjuncts (not four) because redundancy IS byte-
# equality between two byte-strings + one keyset-membership check;
# the substrate does not need a wider conjunction to name it.
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: composition of two Rice-safe
# bilaterals; no additional program semantics.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `witnessing=all-two-pass` — the byte-
# level substrate-decl'd marker. When both sub-bilaterals discharge
# Pass on the same record, the realization layer stamps the sentinel;
# discharge is byte-equality.
#
# Load-bearing structural claim: `arm_is_redundant_witnessing(record)
# = Pass` is the substrate-decl form of "this arm's discharge is
# byte-equal to the reflective evaluator's discharge on the same
# argument list; deletion is safe under the retirement invariant."
# The `collapse` action reads this verdict before dispatching the
# `@io/fs.mutate_at` + `@io/git.commit` composition; failure short-
# circuits deletion + preserves file bytes.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked; realized reflectively via the
# discharge action's `require` closure over the two sub-bilaterals.
bilateral arm_is_redundant_witnessing {
  sentinel "witnessing=all-two-pass"
  arity    1
  require  arm_is_in_reflective_corpus
  require  arm_matches_sentinel
}
arm_is_redundant_witnessing(record: redundant_arm_record) -> verdict { \ }

# === detect action (fracture-emission surface) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING DETECTION ACTION. Reads the bilateral corpus + the
# apply_h.rs bytes; emits one `redundant_arm_record` per hand-typed
# arm shadowed by a corpus entry. Returns empty list when the fixed-
# point holds (no arm shadows any bilateral in the corpus).
#
# Algorithm (per docs/specs/kintsugi-fracture-bilateral-arm-redundant.md
# §3 detection pseudocode):
#
#   detect(apply_h_bytes, corpus):
#     records = []
#     for (action_ref, decl) in corpus.entries():
#       arm_range = grep_for_arm(apply_h_bytes, action_ref)
#       if arm_range is None:
#         continue  # no shadow arm; corpus entry is already terminal
#       arm_sentinel = extract_contains_argument(
#         apply_h_bytes, arm_range
#       )
#       record = redundant_arm_record {
#         action_ref:     action_ref,
#         apply_h_path:   "bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs",
#         arm_line_start: arm_range.line_start,
#         arm_line_end:   arm_range.line_end,
#         sentinel:       decl.sentinel,
#         arm_bytes:      apply_h_bytes[arm_range.byte_start..
#                                        arm_range.byte_end],
#       }
#       if arm_is_redundant_witnessing(record) == Pass:
#         records.append(record)
#     return records
#
# Composition surface:
#   @io/fs.read(apply_h_path)                   — read the resolver bytes
#   @epistemologic/pact/bilateral.load_corpus   — the reflective corpus
#   arm_is_redundant_witnessing(record)         — witnessing conjunction
#
# Rice-safe bound at whole-tick altitude: reads only byte-visible
# state (corpus keyset; apply_h.rs bytes; substring containment); no
# program semantics.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked; Reed follow-up tick A wires the
# roomba composition edge that dispatches this action per bump-
# pulse. The realisation composes over `@io/fs.read` + the corpus
# loader; grep_for_arm + extract_contains_argument are byte-level
# substring operations at @nl altitude.
detect(apply_h_bytes: ref, corpus: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === collapse action (fracture-resolution surface) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING RESOLUTION ACTION. Reads one `redundant_arm_record`;
# byte-deletes the arm via `@io/fs.mutate_at` (empty replacement);
# commits the deletion via `@io/git.commit` under mirror-authorship.
# Returns `@glass.verdict`.
#
# Algorithm (per docs/specs/kintsugi-fracture-bilateral-arm-redundant.md
# §4 resolution pseudocode):
#
#   collapse(record):
